dvy|n|In the form of, or bounded by, a circle; round. ; repeating itself; ending in itself; reverting to the point of beginning; hence, illogical; inconclusive; as, circular reasoning. ; Adhering to a fixed circle of legends; cyclic; hence, mean; inferior. See Cyclic poets, under Cyclic. ; Addressed to a circle, or to a number of persons having a common interest; circulated, or intended for circulation; as, a circular letter. ; Perfect; complete. ; A circular letter, or paper, usually printed, copies of which are addressed or given to various persons; as, a business circular. ; A sleeveless cloak, cut in circular form.	V:1tvw,40,1~1tvw,40,1
